lldepth, header(\"DEBUG\", fmt.Sprint(v...)))\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc (l *DefaultLogger) Debugf(format string, v ...interface{}) {\n\tif l.debug {\n\t\tl.Output(calldepth, header(\"DEBUG\", fmt.Sprintf(format, v...)))\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc (l *DefaultLogger) Info(v ...interface{}) {\n\tl.Output(calldepth, header(\"INFO\", fmt.Sprint(v...)))\n}\n\nfunc (l *DefaultLogger) Infof(format string, v ...interface{}) {\n\tl.Output(calldepth, header(\"INFO\", fmt.Sprintf(format, v...)))\n}\n\nfunc (l *DefaultLogger) Error(v ...interface{}) {\n\tl.Output(calldepth, header(\"ERROR\", fmt.Sprint(v...)))\n}\n\nfunc (l *DefaultLogger) Errorf(format string, v ...interface{}) {\n\tl.Output(calldepth, header(\"ERROR\", fmt.Sprintf(format, v...)))\n}\n\nfunc (l *DefaultLogger) Warning(v ...interface{}) {\n\tl.Output(calldepth, header(\"WARN\", fmt.Sprint(v...)))\n}\n\nfunc (l *DefaultLogger) Warningf(format string, v ...interface{}) {\n\tl.Output(calldepth, header(\"WARN\", fmt.Sprintf(format, v...)))\n}\n\nfunc (l *DefaultLogger) Fatal(v ...interface{}) {\n\tl.Output(calldepth, header(\"FATAL\", fmt.Sprint(v...)))\n\tos.Exit(1)\n}\n\nfunc (l *DefaultLogger) Fatalf(format string, v ...interface{}) {\n\tl.Output(calldepth, header(\"FATAL\", fmt.Sprintf(format, v...)))\n\tos.Exit(1)\n}\n\nfunc (l *DefaultLogger) Panic(v ...interface{}) {\n\tl.Logger.Panic(v...)\n}\n\nfunc (l *DefaultLogger) Panicf(format string, v ...interface{}) {\n\tl.Logger.Panicf(format, v...)\n}\n\nfunc header(lvl, msg string) string {\n\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%s: %s\", lvl, msg)\n}\nfunc stepFollower(r *raft, m pb.Message) error {\n\tswitch m.Type {\n\tcase pb.MsgProp:\n\t\tif r.lead == None {\n\t\t\tr.logger.Infof(\"%x no leader at term %d; dropping proposal\", r.id, r.Term)\n\t\t\treturn ErrProposalDropped\n\t\t} else if r.disableProposalForwarding {\n\t\t\tr.logger.Infof(\"%x not forwarding to leader %x at term %d; dropping proposal\", r.id, r.lead, r.Term)\n\t\t\treturn ErrProposalDropped\n\t\t}\n\t\tm.To = r.lead\n\t\tr.send(m)\n\tcase pb.MsgApp:\n\t\tr.electionElapsed = 0\n\t\tr.lead = m.From\n\t\tr.handleAppendEntries(m)\n\tcase pb.MsgHeartbeat:\n\t\tr.electionElapsed = 0\n\t\tr.lead = m.From\n\t\tr.handleHeartbeat(m)\n\tcase pb.MsgSnap:\n\t\tr.electionElapsed = 0\n\t\tr.lead = m.From\n\t\tr.handleSnapshot(m)\n\tcase pb.MsgTransferLeader:\n\t\tif r.lead == None {\n\t\t\tr.logger.Infof(\"%x no leader at term %d; dropping leader transfer msg\", r.id, r.Term)\n\t\t\treturn nil\n\t\t}\n\t\tm.To = r.lead\n\t\tr.send(m)\n\tcase pb.MsgForgetLeader:\n\t\tif r.readOnly.option == ReadOnlyLeaseBased {\n\t\t\tr.logger.Error(\"ignoring MsgForgetLeader due to ReadOnlyLeaseBased\")\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"The fixed monitor recorded a violation: after transfer expired, the two state snapshots were identical while `AutoLeave` remained true. Every cycle round drained, and the cycle carried only heartbeat messages and replies.\n\nThe source trace supports repeating that suffix: heartbeats keep the quorum active and reset follower election timers, but neither heartbeat processing nor transfer abort invokes the missing exit retry. The control and later proposal both complete exit, so the observed defect is conditional on the failed transfer and absence of later application work.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > make_review.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nrationale='''Reviewed fixed artifact dddede686d1a4bdb87cd514ac7e8f137 version 1, its accepted claim/bindings version 1, fixed plan and complete harness, and retained execution 5ef2409f00cd47c983439ae485dde415. The measured event implication is violated; Go tests_passed only means the observation harness completed.\n\nResponsibility: s_joint_contract and s_conf_contract assign implicit exit to Raft, contrasting explicit exit assigned to the application. s_auto_ownership requires automatic transition when possible. Generic proposal retry language does not make an unrelated ordinary proposal a prerequisite of that owned transition. The observation is not an invented ten-tick deadline: the witness is a recurrent legal execution after transfer expiration.\n\nEntry and history: all three RawNodes start from the same declared index-1/term-1 agreed snapshot and HardState, with no crash. A real Campaign elects node 1 at term 2 and commits/applies its empty entry at index 2. Actual ProposeConfChange creates the implicit removal at index 3. The application starts transfer to node 2 only after observing this committed entry and checking node 2 Match equals the leader tail. The call is serialized between Ready and Advance, with entries already persisted. This permits the relevant overlap rather than draining it away. The leader then applies the committed change and Advance completes application; the active transfer causes the generated exit proposal to be rejected by the ordinary proposal handler. Exactly one actually emitted MsgTimeoutNow is lost, with all later messages delivered through the same queue. No fabricated network support or private protocol writes occur. Synchronous MemoryStorage represents completed storage in this no-crash scope. All Ready work is persisted before delivery and applied before Advance; RawNode has no independent goroutine or shutdown work. This meets the stricter Ready contract as well as the general usage instructions.\n\nCorrelation and admission: overlap=true selects the principal scenario independently of results. case_id plus config_index identifies the same operation in admitted, cycle_start and cycle_result; there is one of each in this history. Admission actually records implicit=true, applied=3, auto_leave=true, transfer=2, one loss and drained work. cycle_start follows the admitted applied value by reference and records transfer=0, leader=true and drained work. Actual configuration events show incoming voters [1,2] and outgoing [1,2,3] on all participants. The result records cycle_closed=true and auto_leave=true, so the independently monitored implication fails. The control is excluded by its predeclared overlap=false, not by whether it succeeded.\n\nObservation and recurrence: I reassembled the retained Go JSON Output chunks and independently parsed both before/after strings; they are equal in the principal scenario. These are fresh immutable snapshots read from the live RawNodes, not cached exports. The recursive traversal includes RawNode previous states and stepsOnAdvance, raft term/vote/role/timers/read queues, log indexes and unstable state, full MemoryStorage hard state/snapshot/entries, membership, progress, inflight buffer and accounting, and caller loss policy and queue. All nodes are term 2 with applied=applying=commit=last=3, no unstable entries or pending snapshots, no Ready/messages/Advance callbacks, and empty transport. Leader progress for all voters is Match=3, Next=4, StateReplicate, RecentActive=true, with zero inflight count/bytes. Automatic-exit size accounting is uncommittedSize=0; pendingConfIndex=3 and applied=3 satisfy its configuration eligibility. Transfer is zero. The only excluded fields are logger/traceLogger, MemoryStorage read callStats and its unlocked mutex. Source shows these counters are increment-only diagnostics, logging is an output sink, default tracing is inactive, and all storage calls here are serialized. Slice capacities and pointer allocation identities do not select the heartbeat-only behavior; the same raft receivers, role callbacks and storage objects remain installed.\n\nThe suffix is ten repetitions of Tick for nodes 1,2,3 followed by complete processing of every Ready and network message. Every round is observed drained and carries only MsgHeartbeat/MsgHeartbeatResp; none is dropped. At each boundary follower electionElapsed is zero because heartbeats reset it. Leader heartbeatElapsed is zero and electionElapsed returns to zero after its configured quorum-check period. Heartbeat replies keep all voters active, so CheckQuorum does not change role. Both quorum sets are available. The captured randomized election timeouts are unchanged and no election threshold is reached; global randomness is only consumed by resetRandomizedElectionTimeout, unreachable on these same-term heartbeat paths. No callbacks, timers, transport work or application work are withheld. Internal MsgBeat and MsgCheckQuorum are generated by Tick, processed synchronously and accounted for by source tracing. The finite harness loop's stop counter merely chooses observation boundaries; it does not influence the target or message policy. Its diagnostic counters and observation flags likewise do not schedule target work. Thus the same external tick schedule can repeat with the same relevant state and effects. With last index fixed and no pending log/application work, no hidden exit proposal is waiting to commit. This closes the continuation premise for the selected history rather than deriving nontermination from finite waiting alone.\n\nCause and counterevidence: appliedTo proposes empty exit but Step rejects while leadTransferee is nonzero; abortLeaderTransfer clears only that blocker. Empty Ready/Advance does not manufacture MsgStorageApplyResp, and heartbeat processing supplies no configuration retry. The 